WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:02.450
- When a great story catches
my eye on the internet,

00:00:02.450 --> 00:00:05.050
I like to serve it up here.
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:08.333 --> 00:00:10.960
A New Hampshire woman had
every reason to freak out

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:14.540
when she awoke to an intruder
in her house, as you would,

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:16.707
but it wasn't a burglar, it was a bear.

00:00:16.707 --> 00:00:19.770
Which is scarier. I think maybe.

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:21.670
Just checking these photos out.

00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:24.010
The furry guest trashed
the front of the house,

00:00:24.010 --> 00:00:27.333
ripping out the walls
and eating insulation.

00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:30.500
The woman's husband
managed to get the bear out

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:31.590
without incident,

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:35.320
but not before it left
thousands of dollars in damages.

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:36.830
We have that woman on the line right now.

00:00:36.830 --> 00:00:40.800
So everybody say hi to Melissa
who watches on NBC Boston.

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:42.123
What's up Melissa?

00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:45.270
- Hi Kelly.

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:48.230
- I mean, so is this like a normal thing

00:00:48.230 --> 00:00:51.048
in your neighborhood?
Like bears in houses?

00:00:51.048 --> 00:00:52.189
- No.

00:00:52.189 --> 00:00:53.210
- Okay.

00:00:53.210 --> 00:00:55.580
- The bears are outside,
yes, that's a normal thing,

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:58.190
but bears in the house? Not so much.

00:00:58.190 --> 00:01:01.524
- Yeah. I'm like that's a big
old bear. He found the honey.

00:01:01.524 --> 00:01:04.543
So wait, what did you guys do?

00:01:06.110 --> 00:01:09.150
- First off we called the police
who called the game warden

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:11.020
who kind of said, well, it's gonna take,

00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:12.190
we live in the middle of nowhere,

00:01:12.190 --> 00:01:15.010
and it was gonna take him
quite some time to get to us.

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:17.460
And he says, well, I'll
gear up and head your way.

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:19.530
He wasn't at all happy about it.

00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:23.100
And he says, I'm gonna call
you before I leave my driveway

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:24.670
and we'll see where we're at.

00:01:24.670 --> 00:01:27.230
And in the meantime, my husband
did not wait with the bear

00:01:27.230 --> 00:01:28.270
'cause it was just getting worse,

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:30.002
and there was the potential

00:01:30.002 --> 00:01:31.550
that he could have come
through the dining room window

00:01:31.550 --> 00:01:33.182
actually into the house.

00:01:33.182 --> 00:01:36.290
So we were just trying to
figure out ways to get him out.

00:01:36.290 --> 00:01:37.570
And I said, well just jump out the window

00:01:37.570 --> 00:01:38.960
and open the door for him.

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:41.020
And he's like, Melissa, it's
eight feet off the ground,

00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:42.960
I'm not jumping out the window.

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:45.500
And then so, but we remembered
there's a ladder on the roof

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:47.331
'cause we had been doing the chimney work.

00:01:47.331 --> 00:01:51.190
So he decided that he would
go upstairs to the bedroom

00:01:51.190 --> 00:01:54.090
and climb out that window
and open the door for him.

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:56.170
And he did, he was able to open the door,

00:01:56.170 --> 00:01:57.614
and finally he left.

00:01:57.614 --> 00:02:01.300
And what surprised me the most
about him leaving was that

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:02.770
he could have gone left or right

00:02:02.770 --> 00:02:04.660
and kind of darted off into the woods,

00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:07.570
but he walked up the
stairs to our driveway.

00:02:07.570 --> 00:02:08.810
You have to go up a few stairs

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:10.500
to get to the top of our driveway.

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:13.300
He walked up the stairs as
though he'd been there before,

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:16.690
he knew that yard, he knew those stairs.

00:02:16.690 --> 00:02:18.347
So I don't think this was his first visit,

00:02:18.347 --> 00:02:20.830
just the first time he
got trapped in the house.

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:22.590
- Well, my personal
favorite part of the story

00:02:22.590 --> 00:02:24.470
is when you thought your
husband was some kind of ninja

00:02:24.470 --> 00:02:26.951
that was gonna jump out
an eight foot window.

00:02:26.951 --> 00:02:28.810
That's my favorite part.

00:02:28.810 --> 00:02:31.913
You were just like jump out
the window and handle it, son.

00:02:33.611 --> 00:02:38.300
- If I could hold the door and
keep a 400 pound bear back,

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:40.593
he should have been able
to jump out the window.

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:47.460
- I love you. Thank you so much,

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:49.300
I'm so happy that y'all
are both all right.

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:52.200
This is a very funny story
because nothing bad happened,

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:54.230
but, and not funny, 'cause it
probably was very expensive

00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:57.143
but I'm liking your post
right now. That's a big bear.

00:02:58.746 --> 00:03:00.010
- [Melissa] Thank you so much.

00:03:00.010 --> 00:03:02.040
- Well thank you so
much, and that's not all,

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:03.440
I want you to know our season long partner

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:04.810
Pilot Pen, makers of Frixion,

00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:07.030
the go-to erasable pen of
"The Kelly Clarkson Show",

00:03:07.030 --> 00:03:09.960
think that your experience is
just as wild as everyone does.

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:11.670
So they're gonna give you $1000.

00:03:11.670 --> 00:03:13.514
Maybe that'll help with
some of the damage.

00:03:13.514 --> 00:03:16.069
- Oh my goodness.

00:03:16.069 --> 00:03:17.490
- [Kelly] All right,
thank you so much Melissa.

00:03:17.490 --> 00:03:19.240
- [Melissa] Well thank you so much.

